{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-qwen3.8-27b-xhigh-yarn1m-full200-2026-09-22","prediction_set_name":"qwen3.8-27b-xhigh-yarn1m-full200-2026-09-22","paper_id":"2601.10950","judge_input_sha256":"842025a52c530a28f006de6233421aa1dfcde658383f9a4b625a6dedbad56e49","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I002:U001","2601.10950:I002:U003","2601.10950:I002:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U004"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the false necessity implication from bare specular differentiability to existence of both one-sided derivatives. ISSUE-001 instead concerns domain and well-formedness defects in a composite-function example; it does not recognize the missing one-sided derivative hypothesis.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I003:U001","2601.10950:I003:U006","2601.10950:I003:U008"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U004"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is nonexistence of the scaled specular derivative for an otherwise admissible function, causing an unconditional theorem input to be undefined. ISSUE-001 identifies an ill-formed derivative expression and an out-of-domain evaluation, not failure of existence of the theorem's scaled derivative under its stated assumptions.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I004:U001","2601.10950:I004:U002","2601.10950:I004:U010"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U003","ISSUE-003:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns deleting signs when converting signed scalar quasi-MVT information into a two-sided norm estimate. ISSUE-003 concerns a separate convexity proposition and invalid substitutions or inequality direction in its proof; it does not diagnose the unsupported norm lower bound.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-005","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I005:U001","2601.10950:I005:U003","2601.10950:I005:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-005:U001","ISSUE-005:U003","ISSUE-005:U004"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"Both concern the S-SPEG algorithm, but the gold defect is the false unbiasedness identity for uniformly sampled component specular gradients. ISSUE-005 only identifies the reversed stopping-condition comparison and does not recognize the estimator expectation failure.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I006","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I006:U001","2601.10950:I006:U003","2601.10950:I006:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U003","ISSUE-003:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the missing uniform subgradient bound needed to justify divergence of the rescaled step sum in the convergence proof. ISSUE-003 concerns a different theorem's convexity proof and does not identify this missing boundedness argument.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I007","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I007:U001","2601.10950:I007:U002","2601.10950:I007:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U003","ISSUE-003:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the invalid promotion of convergence of a subsequence to convergence of the full iterate sequence, with a specific tail-index repair. ISSUE-003 addresses unrelated subgradient substitutions and inequality signs in a convexity proof.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I008","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-005","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I008:U001","2601.10950:I008:U002","2601.10950:I008:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-005:U001","ISSUE-005:U003","ISSUE-005:U004"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns a sample-dependent normalized step that cannot be factored out of conditional expectation, invalidating the descent inequality. ISSUE-005 concerns only the reversed stopping condition in Algorithm 2 and does not recognize the normalization/conditioning error.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2601.10950:I009","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2601.10950:I009:U001","2601.10950:I009:U002","2601.10950:I009:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U003","ISSUE-003:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the invalid inference from a weighted sum bound to a pointwise expected objective-gap bound; only a minimum-over-iterates conclusion follows. ISSUE-003 concerns a separate convexity proof and does not identify this weighted-average versus pointwise error.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}